----- stdout -----
An opinionated Markdown note-taking and management CLI.

Usage: ntropy [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  init       Initialize a vault (idempotent)
  new        Create a note from a template and open it
  today      Open today's note, creating it from the `today` template if absent
  search     Browse, filter, full-text search, or open a note by id or query [alias: list]
  write      Replace one note's content with text read from stdin
  reconcile  Realign drifted filenames, re-sync views, and sync `.gitignore`
  delete     Delete a note by id or query
  render     Render a note to a document artifact
  site       Export the vault as a static website
  view       Manage materialized view definitions
  tags       List all tags with note counts
  info       Show the active vault, its resolution, and vault statistics
  unlock     Store the vault's identity so later commands need no passphrase
  lock       Forget the stored identity, so reading requires the passphrase again
  vault      Whole-vault operations: converting storage and managing the key
  lsp        Run the language server over stdin/stdout
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --vault <PATH>            Operate on the vault at this path (overrides all other resolution)
  -n, --non-interactive         Force non-interactive (plain) behavior even on a TTY
      --strict                  Treat malformed/badly-named notes as errors instead of warnings
  -i, --identity <PATH>         Use this age identity file instead of the OS credential store
      --passphrase-file <PATH>  Read the vault passphrase from the first line of this file
  -h, --help                    Print help (see more with '--help')
  -V, --version                 Print version


----- stderr -----
